# `limit > 100` in every turn, of a parameter of which nothing is known: the relation as written may run other code (a valueOf), which ends in every turn what is shown of the lists that the loop reads.
# A value that no turn changes, of which nothing is expected, and which every turn holds against a number by a relation is asked once in front of the loop whether it is a number; in the copy behind the yes the relation is one of numbers.
